	shorttitle = {{PARP} inhibitors in the management of breast cancer},
	abstract = {Poly({ADP}-ribose) polymerases ({PARP}) are enzymes involved in {DNA}-damage repair. Inhibition of {PARPs} is a promising strategy for targeting cancers with defective {DNA}-damage repair, including {BRCA}1 and {BRCA}2 mutation-associated breast and ovarian cancers. Several {PARP} inhibitors are currently in trials in the adjuvant, neoadjuvant, and metastatic settings for the treatment of ovarian, {BRCA}-mutated breast, and other cancers. We herein review the development of {PARP} inhibitors and the basis for the excitement surrounding these agents, their use as single agents and in combinations, as well as their toxicities, mechanisms of acquired resistance, and companion diagnostics.},
