	abstract = {Oncogenic mutations of {BRAF}, the most frequently mutated protein kinase in human cancers, are particularly common in melanoma and found in more than 40\% of patients. The development of inhibitors targeting {BRAF} is of particular interest as the growth of {BRAF} mutant melanoma cells seems to be dependent on the {RAF}–{MEK}–{ERK} signalling pathway.},
