	abstract = {When ectopically overexpressed, anticancer genes, such as {TRAIL}, {PAR}4 and {ORCTL}3, specifically destroy tumour cells without harming untransformed cells. Anticancer genes can not only serve as powerful tumour specific therapy tools but studying their mode of action can reveal mechanisms underlying the neoplastic transformation, sustenance and spread.},
