	issn = {1748-717X},
	url = {https://doi.org/10.1186/1748-717X-7-1},
	doi = {10.1186/1748-717X-7-1},
	abstract = {For studying proliferation and determination of survival of cancer cells after irradiation, the multiple {MTT} assay, based on the reduction of a yellow water soluble tetrazolium salt to a purple water insoluble formazan dye by living cells was modified from a single-point towards a proliferation assay. This assay can be performed with a large number of samples in short time using multi-well-plates, assays can be performed semi-automatically with a microplate reader. Survival, the calculated parameter in this assay, is determined mathematically. Exponential growth in both control and irradiated groups was proven as the underlying basis of the applicability of the multiple {MTT} assay. The equivalence to a clonogenic survival assay with its disadvantages such as time consumption was proven in two setups including plating of cells before and after irradiation. Three cell lines (A 549, {LN} 229 and F 98) were included in the experiment to study its principal and general applicability.},
